m H001 and H002, using the declared smoothness and permitted finite-dimensional differentiation/inner-product calculations. No unsupported mathematical implication was found. The packet nevertheless fails object closure: the proof actually uses existential witness a from H002 but has no local declaration for it. This is an omission, not a finding that the underlying implication is false. Input boundary: the complete packet and the declared Yui Audit A/self-containment/format rules; no source proof or other mathematical material was used. This is a fresh review of the supplied packet in this context. I make no claim about carrier identity, canonical hash binding, transmitted-material readback, runtime isolation, or external attestation; those are outside the mathematical review.\",\"checks\":{\"inputs\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"H001 supplies unit norm at every allowed point; H002 supplies the pointwise existential equation. Both are instantiated at the arbitrary x,r fixed by S001, with compatible declared domains.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs/0/statement\",\"/inputs/1/statement\",\"/inference/argument/0/uses\"]},\"argument\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"For fixed x and r>0, smoothness of u and the permitted finite-dimensional differentiation/inner-product identities justify differentiating |u|²=1 to get 2u·u_t=0, hence u·u_t=0. H002 gives the equation at that point; taking inner product with u_t yields the requested zero identity. The witness scalar needs no regularity. The calculation proves the output for the arbitrary point.\",\"locations\":[\"/parameters/2/type\",\"/logic/calculations/0\",\"/inputs/0/statement\",\"/inputs/1/statement\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\"]},\"dependency_accounting\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"H001 is used for the differentiated unit-norm identity and H002 for the pointwise equation. No named analysis theorem or additional factual premise is hidden in the calculation; the existential witness is supplied by H002, although its missing local declaration is separately a closure defect.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/inputs\",\"/inference/argument/0/uses\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\"]},\"output\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The argument establishes u_t(x,r)·(u_tt(x,r)−Δ_xu(x,r))=0 at each arbitrary x∈ℝⁿ and r>0, matching the full output statement; no extra condition, endpoint, or constant is introduced.\",\"locations\":[\"/output/statement\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\"]},\"scope\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The arbitrary x and positive r are fixed for the single step and the conclusion is stated universally. The existential scalar is used only for the pointwise calculation and does not escape into the output. The text indicates local existential use (“at this point”), though the corresponding object declaration is missing and causes object_closure to fail.\",\"locations\":[\"/inference/locals/0\",\"/inference/locals/1\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/output/statement\"]},\"applicability\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"There are no E or M inputs or source-theorem obligations. H001 and H002 are applied at the fixed admissible point; their stated universal domains include it.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs/0/statement\",\"/inputs/1/statement\",\"/inference/argument/0/uses\"]},\"statement_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The input and output propositions state their formulas and relevant quantification/domain conditions in the packet. D003 defines Δ_x as the componentwise sum of second spatial derivatives, and the parameter declaration supplies the map and its domain. H001's “x,r>0” is read with the declared x∈ℝⁿ and r>0 parameter domains.\",\"locations\":[\"/parameters\",\"/definitions/0\",\"/inputs/0/statement\",\"/inputs/1/statement\",\"/output/statement\"]},\"object_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"FAIL\",\"notes\":\"The prose uses the scalar a in “H002 supplies a scalar a at this point” and subsequently forms a(u_t·u). H002 does provide an existentially bound scalar, so its existence is grounded, but a is absent from the inference locals and the prose does not give a complete local declaration/type/scope record for it. The registered locals x and r do not account for this actual object occurrence. This is the first closure defect; it does not by itself invalidate the mathematical calculation.\",\"locations\":[\"/inputs/1/statement\",\"/inference/locals\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\"]},\"dependency_closure\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"The facts used in the prose trace to H001, H002, the declared smoothness, and the explicitly permitted differentiation and inner-product calculations. The value a is sourced from H002's existential statement; no ancestor proof or outside premise is needed. Its declaration bookkeeping defect is recorded under object_closure.\",\"locations\":[\"/parameters/2/type\",\"/logic/calculations/0\",\"/inputs/0/statement\",\"/inputs/1/statement\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\"]},\"packet_replay\":{\"verdict\":\"PASS\",\"notes\":\"I read the full frozen packet and the relevant declared Audit A, self-containment, and format rules, and assessed this inference using only those materials. On that mathematical-input boundary the packet contains sufficient premises and definitions to assess the calculation and exposes the undeclared witness defect. No carrier/runtime attestation is inferred from this review; carrier identity, hash binding, and transmitted-material readback are outside this mathematical judgment.\",\"locations\":[\"/packet_sha256\",\"/inputs\",\"/definitions/0\",\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"/inference/locals\"]}},\"findings\":[{\"location\":\"/inference/argument/0/text\",\"issue\":\"Object-closure omission: the proof uses existential witness a supplied by H002, but a has no inference-local declaration in /inference/locals. The witness is mathematically available from H002 and the calculation is valid; the packet does not meet the required actual-object declaration closure.\"}]}}"